# .gitignore for dex-forge
#
# The guiding rule: track anything a fresh clone needs in order to train, evaluate
# or deploy. Do not track anything a training run produces -- those are large,
# regenerable, and were the reason `git status` used to list 700+ entries.
#
# See docs/REPO_LAYOUT.md for what each top-level directory is actually for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
wheelhouse/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / lint / type-check caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training and experiment output
#
# runs/ holds every RL-Games checkpoint and is the single biggest directory in a
# working copy (tens of GB), so it is ignored wholesale.
#
# Three files under runs/ are nevertheless tracked -- the published HORA ep-760
# policy, its Stage-2 deploy bundle, and the adaptation validation report -- because
# deployment depends on those exact weights. They stay tracked because .gitignore
# does not apply to files git already knows about. Note that a `!runs/...` negation
# would NOT work here: git will not re-include anything beneath an excluded
# directory. To publish another policy, force it in with `git add -f <path>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
logs/
checkpoints/
wandb/
outputs/
deliverables/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console logs and recorded telemetry
#
# Training is normally launched as `... > stage1.log 2>&1 &`, and the deploy tools
# record CSV traces. Both land at the repo root and are pure run output; a single
# stage-1 log reached 98 MB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local hardware captures and debug renders
#
# Root level only: curated renders committed under artifacts/ must stay tracked,
# so these patterns are anchored with a leading slash.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.mov
/*.MOV
/*.webm
# One-off pose/readback dumps written by the hand_check and posture tools.
/decoded_pose*.json
/posed_state.json
/startup*.json
/*_readback.json
/topdown_*_pose.json
/wiggle_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3D-printing output (generated plates and slicer output, not source CAD)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
print/
*.3mf
*.gcode

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merge/patch conflict backups -- these caused real confusion (a README.md.orig
# and train.py.orig sat at the root for weeks looking like live files).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS, and a scratch area for throwaway work
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
_scratch/
